<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iziaslav I of Kiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1024–1078</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Iziaslav Yaroslavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iziaslav I was grand prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and the eldest surviving son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a>, succeeding him in 1054. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> defeated him on the Alta River in 1068 the people of Kiev drove him out; he returned with Polish help, was expelled again by his brothers in 1073 and regained the throne in 1077. He was killed in 1078 fighting his nephews at Nezhatina Niva.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iziaslav-i-of-kiev.jpg" alt="Iziaslav I of Kiev" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Izyaslav_I_with_his_portrait.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
